# cmd.exe parses a batch file by its line endings, and an LF-only one can fail
# in ways that look like the script itself is broken. `eol=crlf` keeps these
# CRLF in the working tree on every platform, whatever core.autocrlf happens to
# be set to on the machine doing the checkout — which is the setting nobody
# remembers and the reason "it works on my machine" has a Windows chapter.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# The shell scripts are for macOS and Linux. A Windows clone with autocrlf on
# would otherwise hand CRLF to bash, where `set -euo pipefail` and friends
# dislike a stray carriage return as much as you would.
*.sh text eol=lf
